      "id": "claim_55a89948e12b4245a52a7ecddc45ddd8",
      "statement": "The default branch is not a working branch: every change, including a one-line fix, must go through a pull request so it is reviewed, and the contract prescribes the exact sequence of branch, regenerate, check, commit, local review, push and open the pull request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L165-L185",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3ab0e73f8c6e252c2cf6d094c43511a684558c1f8d6f324526f69ec47a7e34a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53ccf434c27848c1922cad49a10156cf",
      "statement": "Running the command-line reviewer before every push is required rather than optional, because the hosted reviewer runs after the push, applies the configuration from the base branch rather than the branch under review, and can refuse for the day on a public repository once its review limit is reached.",
      "evidence": [
        {
